---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "September 11, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use — Dinkly"
  description="The terms governing use of Dinkly: acceptable use, intellectual property, entertainment-only disclaimers, and limitation of liability."
>
  <div class="wrap narrow page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <span>Terms of Use</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="head">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        By using Dinkly you agree to these terms. They are written to be readable, and the short version is:
        use the site normally, don't abuse it, and remember that the oracle, the quizzes and the cards are
        entertainment rather than professional advice.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        Dinkly is free to use for personal, non-commercial purposes. You may browse, play, share links, and
        save exported wallpapers for personal use including as desktop or phone backgrounds.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or its infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Do not scrape the site at a volume that degrades service for other people.</li>
        <li>Do not resell or repackage Dinkly's content as your own product.</li>
        <li>Do not use automated tools to generate fake traffic or advertising impressions.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Entertainment only</h2>
      <p>
        The Daily Draw, the Yes/No Oracle, the personality quizzes and the jokes are provided purely for
        amusement. They are not psychological assessments, financial advice, medical advice, legal advice,
        or predictions of future events. Do not make significant life decisions on the basis of a card drawn
        by a random number generator.
      </p>
      <p>
        Likewise, nothing on this site is professional advice about work, health or wellbeing. The essays in
        Break Notes reflect general observations, not clinical guidance.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The written content, design, code and generated assets of Dinkly are the property of their respective
        creators. You may quote short excerpts with a link back to the source page. Wholesale reproduction
        requires permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Emoji characters used in the memory game and elsewhere are provided by your device's operating system
        and font vendors, not by Dinkly.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Advertising and third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        The site displays advertising and may link to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the
        content, products, or privacy practices of those third parties. Any transaction you enter into with
        an advertiser is solely between you and them.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        Dinkly is provided "as is". We aim to keep it online and working, but we do not guarantee
        uninterrupted availability, and features may change or be removed. Data stored in your browser's
        local storage may be lost when you clear browsing data or change devices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Dinkly and its creators are not liable for any indirect,
        incidental, or consequential loss arising from your use of, or inability to use, the site —
        including time spent, or not spent, waiting for an AI model to finish.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the site after an update constitutes
        acceptance of the revised terms. Material changes will carry a new "last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be raised through the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 780px; }
  .page { padding: 34px 0 20px; }
  .crumbs { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--faint); display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--muted); }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .head { margin: 28px 0 30px; }
  .head h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .prose { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.76; }
  .prose .lead { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .prose li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent); }
</style>
